The fix is complete. Remaining 5 failures are pre-existing environment issues (DNS/network/external HTTPS), unrelated to the change — baseline had 8 failures including the 3 GZIP decompression tests that now pass.

**Fix** in `lib/adapters/http.js:548-550`: the `content-encoding` response header is now normalized (trimmed + lowercased) before the decompression switch, so values like `GZIP`, `GZip`, or `Br` are handled correctly:

```js
if (config.decompress !== false && res.headers['content-encoding']) {
  // normalize the content-encoding header to lowercase, because it is case-insensitive
  res.headers['content-encoding'] = res.headers['content-encoding'].trim().toLowerCase();
```

This matches the issue report: services like `storage.googleapis.com` send `Content-Encoding: GZIP`, which previously fell through the `switch` and skipped decompression.
